Package: winbridge
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libc6
# openssh-client and rsync drive the optional headless-VM build path used
# for Flutter (`winbridge vm status|doctor`, see docs/vm-setup.md) — most
# installs never touch it, so it is a Recommends, not a Depends.
# curl and xz-utils are what AssetCache (lib/src/run/asset_cache.dart) shells
# out to on first `winbridge run`/`--dxvk`/`prefix tricks`, to download and
# unpack the pinned Wine, DXVK and winetricks archives.
Recommends: openssh-client, rsync, curl, xz-utils
Description: build and run Windows apps from Linux, without leaving Linux
 WinBridge cross-compiles Windows binaries from Go, Rust, .NET, C/C++ and
 Flutter projects and checks every artifact for a real Windows PE32+ header
 before calling a build a success. Native cross-compilers are used wherever
 the language allows it; Flutter, which needs Visual Studio and only runs on
 Windows, is built on a headless VM this tool drives over SSH.
 .
 It also runs existing Windows programs: `winbridge run app.exe` launches a
 Windows binary through a managed Wine runtime this tool downloads and
 verifies itself, with an isolated prefix per app, optional DXVK for
 Direct3D-over-Vulkan rendering, and winetricks for extra runtimes an app
 needs. No system Wine, no root, nothing to configure by hand.
